---
import '../../styles/wellington-glass.css';
import DailyBriefing from "./DailyBriefing.astro";
import AudienceHero from "./AudienceHero.astro";
import SmoothInteractions from "./SmoothInteractions.astro";
import TechnicalFeatures from "./TechnicalFeatures.astro";
const benefits=[
 {title:"Set the boundaries",body:"Define what each agent can access and change, and which actions need approval."},
 {title:"Check what depends on it",body:"See which reports, workflows, or teams a proposed action could affect."},
 {title:"See why it happened",body:"Review what the agent attempted, which facts and rules informed the decision, and what actually ran."}
];
const requests=["Make room for what matters this week.","What have I promised that I haven’t followed through on?","Get everything ready for tomorrow.","Help me pick this project back up.","Who should I reconnect with?","Take care of the routine parts. Bring me the decisions."];
---
<AudienceHero/>
<section class="cp-container cp-section cp-overview" aria-labelledby="cp-overview-heading">
 <div class="cp-center"><h2 id="cp-overview-heading">Give agents room to work. Keep control of what changes.</h2><p>Hand over the recurring work. Keep a say when an action would affect another team, a live report, or a commitment someone is counting on.</p></div>
 <div class="cp-three cp-benefits">{benefits.map((item,index)=><article><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24">{index===0?<><path d="m10.1 10.1-3-3m6.8 3 3-3m-6.8 6.8-3 3m6.8-3 3 3"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2.7"/><circle cx="5" cy="5" r="3"/><circle cx="19" cy="5" r="3"/><circle cx="5" cy="19" r="3"/><circle cx="19" cy="19" r="3"/></>:index===1?<path d="M4 20 20 4M7 4h13v13"/>:<><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="6.5"/><path d="m15 15 5.5 5.5"/></>}</svg><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.body}</p></article>)}</div>
</section>

<section class="cp-container cp-section cp-usecases" aria-labelledby="cp-usecases-heading">
 <h2 class="cp-center" id="cp-usecases-heading">One workspace model across agents.</h2>
 <p class="cp-sapiens-direction">Every agent works in the same business, even when it uses a different tool. Wellington is designed to share the context that matters across those tools: who owns a resource, what depends on it, and who can approve a change.</p>
 <div class="cp-three cp-ruled">
  <article><h3>Know what depends on what</h3><p>A weekly report can still rely on a folder that looks ready to archive.</p></article>
  <article><h3>Use that context across agents</h3><p>The same dependency matters whether a cleanup agent proposes the archive or a colleague asks an assistant to do it.</p></article>
  <article><h3>Show the reason for review</h3><p>The person responsible would see the proposed change, the work it could affect, and what Wellington still needs to verify.</p></article>
 </div>
</section>
<div class="cp-container cp-briefing">
 <DailyBriefing/>
</div>
<section class="cp-container cp-section cp-split cp-hood" aria-labelledby="cp-hood-heading">
 <div>
  <h2 id="cp-hood-heading">What’s under the hood.</h2>
  <a class="btn cp-button" href="https://innovatingfuture.com/ai-lab/#harness">Explore the architecture</a>
 </div>
 <div class="cp-hood-points">
  <article><h3>Map the workspace</h3><p>Connectors would supply facts about resources, owners and dependencies.</p></article>
  <article><h3>Reason about effects</h3><p>Before a call runs, Wellington would follow those dependencies to assess what else could change.</p></article>
  <article><h3>Surface what’s unknown</h3><p>If the facts needed for a decision are missing or conflicting, Wellington would hold the call for review.</p></article>
 </div>
</section>
<TechnicalFeatures/>
<SmoothInteractions/>

